First step of #12

- Read-Only tables

Why read-only?
------------------

For example, let us consider following schema:

```
SCHEMA ap000;
  ENTITY a;
    x: INTEGER;
    y: INTEGER;
  END_ENTITY;

  ENTITY b;
    z: INTEGER;
    w: a;
  END_ENTITY;

  ENTITY c;
    p: a;
    q: b;
  END_ENTITY;
END_SCHEMA;
```

To implement mutable reference in an instance of `c`, we have to determine `c.p` and `c.q.w` are same or different data to ensure the single `&mut` rule of Rust. I postpone this feature to future Pull Request.

